nodecode-skill-matcher is a rewrite of xXLODXx's xXLODXx/hermes-skill-router:

  https://github.com/xXLODXx/hermes-skill-router
  commit 445c32f9b274f53bf3d37ce1b37ec1b3e5530ac4
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Skill Router contributors (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp as a Nodecode cell: the evidence-first scoring is
the original's (a word shared with a name 5, a tag 3, a description 1, a
stem or compound overlap only supporting evidence, confidence the score over
ten plus a little for agreeing kinds, a floor of 3, at most three named,
the rest reported as rejections, and the same fallback line). Its catalog is
this organism's own inventory -- the cell folders under the home and every
SKILL.md beneath them -- read with a small hand parser instead of the
original's regexes, and it keeps the local decision log, with a hashed
topic signature kept per session so a task routed twice says so.

Left out: the Hermes hook path. The original injected its block into the
first turn of every session by itself, on four Hermes hooks (pre_llm_call,
pre_tool_call, post_tool_call, post_llm_call); a Nodecode cell reaches the
prompt through the harness sections, and no accessor here answers a
session's newest user message, so the rewrite routes on demand -- the
match_skills tool, /skill-matcher, and a manual topic -- rather than
speculating on every turn. Also left out: the keyword learning store
(learned_keywords.json, tool_stats.json) with its lift gate and pruning,
which needs Hermes tool-call names to learn from; and the dashboard
(dashboard/, a React page over a FastAPI router), which has no counterpart
here.
